{
  "name": "443. xAI chat reports server-side tool usage and refuses undeliverable cache fields; Responses takes max_turns (xai chat contract)",
  "description": "Pins TXE-7043 (contract C4, C5; vendor sheet xAI chat B1, B2, responses B3). Local fixture regression, no live provider calls: start tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs, start an isolated gateway on tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json and run with providerErrorFixture=1; every case is skipped otherwise. The xai provider's base is the fixture's /pp/xai, so every vendor call is a row of GET /__wire. Rows 2 and 3: usage.server_side_tool_usage_details, the per-tool call counts xAI reports, is in the chat usage and on the final streamed frame; before the change the field was not in the unified usage at all. Rows 4 to 6: prompt_cache_key and prompt_cache_retention on a model whose capability record does not list them are 400 caller_unsupported_parameter, streamed too; before the change the field was removed and the request sent without it. Rows 7 and 8: max_turns on /v1/responses, with no x-bf-passthrough-extra-params header. Rows 9 to 11 repeat the three behaviours on the OpenAI SDK routes /openai/v1/chat/completions and /openai/v1/responses, with those routes' own request shape: an integration route carries a field it does not model only under extra_params with x-bf-passthrough-extra-params: true, so max_turns is sent that way there. Row 12 reads the wire: max_turns arrived as sent on all three Responses requests (before the change the unified route dropped it without the header), and only the three accepted chat requests reached xAI.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "443.1 reset the fixture's record (xai chat contract)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8791/__reset"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('the fixture reset its record', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "443.2 xai/grok-4.5 POST /v1/chat/completions reports server_side_tool_usage_details in usage (xai chat contract)",
      "request": {
